{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 22, :comments ["<b>The most holy things.</b> These are קָדְשֵׁי הַקֳּדָשִׁים." "<b>And of the holy things he may eat.</b> These are minor holy things. And if קָדְשֵׁי הַקֳּדָשִׁים were stated, why were minor holy things stated? For if they were not stated, I would say: a blemished priest may eat קָדְשֵׁי הַקֳּדָשִׁים — for we find that they were permitted to a non-priest, since Moses ate the flesh of the ordination offerings; but the breast and thigh of minor holy things he may not eat, for we do not find a non-priest sharing in them. Therefore minor holy things were stated. So it is expounded in Zevachim (101a)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:38.273742376Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}